{
  "description": "Full-close days of the US government-securities market, 2018-01-01 to 2027-12-31: the days `data.quarter_end` does not count as business days, besides Saturdays and Sundays. Eleonora's ruling of 1 October 2026 on #44 (option A). An entry with basis 'statute' is a legal public holiday under 5 U.S.C. 6103(a) on its observed day (a Saturday holiday on the Friday before, a Sunday one on the Monday after); tests/test_data.py derives them from the statute and checks this list against the derivation. An entry with basis 'sifma' is a full close SIFMA recommended beyond the statute; verified false means it was not read on sifma.org, which the rmm environment cannot reach. 'statutory_days_the_market_opened' lists observed statutory holidays on which the market did not close; they are not in 'closed'. An unscheduled closure is a new entry, added by a reviewed pull request. data.MARKET_HOLIDAYS_SHA256 pins this file's sha256, and data.quarter_end refuses a file that does not match it, so a changed entry is a reviewed code change too.",
